The pinned source and frozen pnpm lockfile reproduce 45 of the archive's 46 files
byte for byte, including every JS, CSS, HTML, service worker, image and font file.
The remaining CNAME differs only by a terminal newline. See BUILDING.md.
Archive SHA-256: 5ab53b5c2dbee58d2074b00b71f228b3f7c0e748c9ac34501d33b01ef186b7a7
The ZIP comment records deployment commit f2876c17419e95622a78c73d1aba10fda1a14a47
and the archive is dated 2023-06-14. That deployment commit cannot currently be
resolved from the official repository. The equivalent source is not claimed to
recover the unique historical build commit, environment or deployment history.
Complete bundled dependency, icon and font notices are reproduced in
app/src/main/assets/LICENSE, also accessible through the app's license viewer.
The reference build identifies 58 runtime npm components; font licenses are
separate: Inter 3.019 uses OFL-1.1, Roboto Mono 3.000 uses Apache-2.0.
Do not interpret npm CSS package metadata as licensing the font data under MIT.
Two MIT components supply explicit license declarations but no separate LICENSE
file; their pinned declarations, author metadata and standard reference terms
are identified in the application license asset, without invented copyright dates.
The shipped ZIP has not been replaced; yacd.version.txt value 3 remains the
Android asset revision counter, not the UI's semantic version.

